{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Do not be wicked.</b> Since the wickedness of the majority brings a person to danger, he said, \"Why should you die before your time?\" Know that wickedness is to occupy oneself with worldly matters. He said: occupy yourself with what suffices for you, and do not be a fool at all, for folly kills before one's time."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:07.847379346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}